diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
+++ b/README.md
+todo board [--overdue] [--snoozed] [--tag TAG]... [--priority P] [--open|--done] [--search TEXT] [--sort priority|due]   # todo, doing and done side by side
+Shared filters: `--overdue` and `--snoozed` work on `todo board`, `todo list`, `todo search` and `todo export`, next to `--tag`, `--priority`, `--open|--done`, `--search` and `--sort`. `--overdue` shows only open items past their due date. A snoozed item is hidden by default from `todo board`, `todo list`, `todo search`, `todo export` and `todo remind`; `--snoozed` shows only the snoozed ones instead. `todo search TEXT` takes only `--overdue` and `--snoozed` (the same as `todo list --search TEXT`), so `todo search TEXT --snoozed` finds a snoozed item.
+### Board
+
+`todo board` prints the items in three columns side by side: `todo`, `doing` and `done`. It takes the same filters as `todo list` (`--overdue`, `--snoozed`, `--tag`, `--priority`, `--open|--done`, `--search`, `--sort`) and writes nothing.
+
+```
+todo                doing               done
+1 write report      3 review the quar…  4 call mum
+2 buy milk          6 file taxes
+```
+
+- A column is the item's state: `done` for a done item, `doing` for an open item marked as doing, `todo` for every other open item. A done item is never in `doing`.
+- Each cell is `ID title`. The items are the ones `todo list` shows, in the order `todo list` shows them (`--sort due` and `--sort priority` order within each column), so snoozed items are hidden unless you pass `--snoozed`, which shows only the snoozed ones. `--overdue` keeps only open items past their due date, so the `done` column is empty.
+- The three columns share the terminal width, each `(width - 4) // 3` characters wide with two spaces between them. A title that does not fit is cut and ends with `…`. Wide characters (such as Chinese) count as two characters, so a column never runs over. The width comes from your terminal (`$COLUMNS` when set, 80 when it cannot be found).
+- Trailing spaces are cut. A column with fewer items than the others leaves blank cells, and with no items to show it prints only the header line.
+- Below a width of 7 the columns no longer fit, so each line is cut to the width.
+- A bad flag or value exits 2, as in `todo list`.
+
